{"study_accession":"PRJNA808797","secondary_study_accession":"SRP360711","title":"Newly defined human hematopoietic stem cell populations","description":"Transcriptomic profiling (RNA-seq) of primitive human progenitor populations CD34+CD38-CD45RA-CD90-EPCR-; hereafter CD90-EPCR- MPP. Overall design: Purpose: To characterize the transcriptomic profile of the human CD90-EPCR- MPP progenitor population. Methods: Cells were obtained from human cord-blood and flow-sorted using the surface antigens described. 5 CD90-EPCR- biological replicates were used to extract total RNA and quality was verified (RIN >8). Libraries were prepared using 20-25 ng/sample of starting RNA. All samples were sequenced two independent times. Conclusions: This study represents the analysis of transcriptomes from a human progenitor population, with biologic replicates, generated by RNA-seq technology. The optimized data analysis workflows reported here should provide a framework for comparative investigations of expression profiles of other human blood stem/progenitor populations.","pubmed":"35440586","geo_series":"","n_samples":5,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN26106883","study_accession":"PRJNA808797","blood_class":"cord_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"CD90-EPCR- MPP 14","description":"CD90-EPCR- MPP 14","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM5908138","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":2,"first_public":"2022-02-24","attributes":[["source_name","cord blood"],["cell_type","cord blood CD34+CD38-CD45RA-CD90-EPCR- cells"],["age","post-natal"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR18083771","experiment_accession":"SRX14235283","library_layout":"SINGLE","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina HiSeq 4000","read_count":13268824,"base_count":1340151224,"first_public":"2022-02-24","experiment_title":"Illumina HiSeq 4000 sequencing: GSM5908138: CD90-EPCR- MPP 14 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"},{"run_accession":"SRR18083772","experiment_accession":"SRX14235283","library_layout":"SINGLE","library_selection":"c